exports[`what an agent reads, word for word > get_component: Side Navigation props 1`] = `
"# Side Navigation (\`SideNavigation\`) · pattern · stable since 1.0.0
\`import { SideNavigation } from '@idyeah/diya'\` · renders inside DiyaProvider
A vertical app navigation with grouped items and an optional collapsed icon rail; items with \`href\` are links. The ref, \`className\`, \`style\` and other attributes go to the \`nav\`.

When: For moving between the main sections of an app, grouped, with an optional collapsed rail. Five or fewer top-level sections? Site Header’s navigation may be enough.

## Props
- \`groups: readonly SideNavigationGroup[]\` Item groups, in order.
- \`value: string\` The current item's \`value\`; it is marked as the current page.
- \`brand?: ReactNode\` Logo or product name at the top.
- \`collapsed?: boolean = false\` Narrow, icon-only rail; defaults to false.
- \`collapsedBrand?: ReactNode\` Smaller brand shown when collapsed; defaults to \`brand\`.
- \`collapsedFooter?: ReactNode\` Smaller footer shown when collapsed, such as the account Menu with just an Avatar; defaults to \`footer\`.
- \`footer?: ReactNode\` Pinned under the groups, such as an account or workspace Menu; it sits at the bottom when the navigation is given its full height.
- \`label?: string\` Accessible name for the navigation landmark (not shown); defaults to "Application navigation".
- \`onValueChange?: (value: string) => void\` Called with an item's \`value\` when it is chosen; leave it out when every item has an \`href\` and the links do the routing.
- \`showGroups?: boolean = true\` Shows group headings; defaults to true.
Also takes native \`<nav>\` attributes, a ref, \`className\` and \`style\`.

## Content
- \`children\`: not taken
- \`brand\`: text or image, several
- \`collapsedBrand\`: text or image
- \`collapsedFooter\`: menu, avatar, button
- \`footer\`: menu, avatar, button, text-link, several
- \`groups[].items[].icon\`: icon

## State
- Controlled: \`value\` with \`onValueChange\`.

## Types
\`\`\`ts
type SideNavigationGroup = { id: string; label?: string; items: readonly SideNavigationItem[]; }
type SideNavigationItem = { value: string; label: string; icon?: ReactNode; href?: string; disabled?: boolean; count?: number; }
\`\`\`

Catalog: https://diya13.ai/explore?pattern=side-navigation"
`;

exports[`what an agent reads, word for word > get_component: Switch 1`] = `
"# Switch (\`Switch\`) · component · stable since 1.0.0
\`import { Switch } from '@idyeah/diya'\` · renders inside DiyaProvider
An on/off toggle (a native checkbox with role="switch") with a label and optional helper text or error.

When: For a setting that takes effect the moment it flips, like notifications. Part of a form that is saved with a button? A checkbox (Choice with multiple) reads more honestly.

## Props
- \`label: string\` Visible label beside the switch; also its accessible name. Hide it with hideLabel.
- \`checked?: boolean\` Whether the switch is on, when controlled; pair it with \`onCheckedChange\`.
- \`defaultChecked?: boolean\` Whether the switch starts on when uncontrolled; a form reset returns to it.
- \`disabled?: boolean = false\` Prevents toggling and dims the switch.
- \`error?: string\` Visible error message below the label; marks the switch invalid while set.
- \`helperText?: string\` Visible hint below the label, announced with the switch; \`error\` replaces it while set.
- \`hideLabel?: boolean = false\` Hides the label visually but keeps it as the switch's accessible name.
- \`onCheckedChange?: (checked: boolean) => void\` Called with the new on/off state when the switch is toggled.
- \`size?: "small" | "medium" | "large" = 'medium'\` Track and thumb size; defaults to 'medium'.
- \`value?: string\` The value sent with the form under \`name\` while the switch is on; defaults to "on", like a checkbox.
Also takes native \`<input>\` attributes, a ref, \`className\` and \`style\`.

## Content
- \`children\`: not taken

## State
- Controlled: \`checked\` with \`onCheckedChange\`; uncontrolled: \`defaultChecked\`.

## Accessibility
role="switch" with its state announced as on or off. Space toggles it.

## Complete file (\`SwitchExample.tsx\`)
\`\`\`tsx
'use client'

import { useState } from 'react'
import { Switch } from '@idyeah/diya'

export default function SwitchExample() {
  const [notifications, setNotifications] = useState(false)

  return (
    <Switch
      label="Email notifications"
      checked={notifications}
      onCheckedChange={setNotifications}
    />
  )
}
\`\`\`

Catalog: https://diya13.ai/explore?area=components&component=switch"
`;

exports[`what an agent reads, word for word > get_setup: next + tailwind 1`] = `
"# Set up @idyeah/diya 1.1.0 in Next.js (App Router)

## 1. Install
\`\`\`sh
npm install @idyeah/diya
\`\`\`

## 2. app/globals.css (Tailwind v4: DIYA above Tailwind's base, below its utilities)
\`\`\`css
@layer theme, base, diya, components, utilities;
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "@idyeah/diya/styles.css";
\`\`\`

## 3. app/providers.tsx (a client file, so Link and functions can reach the provider)
\`\`\`tsx
'use client'
import Link from 'next/link'
import type { ReactNode } from 'react'
import { DiyaProvider } from '@idyeah/diya'

export function Providers({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return <DiyaProvider linkComponent={Link}>{children}</DiyaProvider>
}
\`\`\`

## 4. app/layout.tsx (the root layout)
\`\`\`tsx
import type { ReactNode } from 'react'
import { Providers } from './providers'
import './globals.css'

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <Providers>{children}</Providers>
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
\`\`\`

## Rules
- Every component renders inside \`DiyaProvider\`; popups, tooltips and toasts need it. Its \`theme\` defaults to \`"system"\` (follows the OS light or dark setting, in CSS, with no flash); pass \`"light"\` or \`"dark"\` to fix it. It paints its own background and text color; \`surface={false}\` leaves that to your page.
- Fields work controlled (\`value\` with \`onValueChange\`; Switch: \`checked\` with \`onCheckedChange\`) or uncontrolled (\`defaultValue\`; Switch: \`defaultChecked\`). Native \`name\`, \`onChange\` and \`onBlur\` reach the native control, so react-hook-form \`register()\` works on TextInput, TextArea, Select, Switch, Choice and Slider without a Controller. Labels are required, even when hidden with \`hideLabel\`.
- Lay screens out with \`Stack\` (vertical) and \`Inline\` (horizontal, wrapping): \`gap\` takes a spacing step (1–8) or any CSS length, plus \`align\`, \`justify\`, \`wrap\` and \`as\`.
- One brand color, set once: \`<DiyaProvider brandColor="#1F4E7A">\`, or \`{ light, dark }\`. Components take no color props (chart series aside); \`tone\` picks a status.
- Every component takes \`className\`, \`style\` and its root element's attributes. Theme with public \`--diya-*\` tokens on \`.diya-root\`, never by overriding internal classes. DIYA's CSS sits in \`@layer diya\`, so your CSS and Tailwind utilities win.
- Links: items with \`href\` render the provider's \`linkComponent\` (such as Next.js \`Link\`, passed from a \`'use client'\` providers file) or a plain anchor. Button takes \`href\` and \`asChild\`. TextLink's \`href\` is always a plain anchor; for client-side routing, pass your router's link to it with \`asChild\`.
- DIYA ships no icon set. Pass any React icon (for example from lucide-react) to icon slots.
- Charts import from \`@idyeah/diya/charts\` and need \`echarts@6\` installed.
- Next.js App Router: DIYA components are client components; a file that passes functions as props needs \`'use client'\`.
- DIYA animates popups, dialogs, toggles and selection, and follows the device's Reduce Motion setting. \`motion="reduced"\` (fades only) or \`"off"\` on DiyaProvider changes it for everything inside; nested providers inherit it. Tune the speed with \`--diya-duration-scale\`. In browser tests, render with \`motion="off"\`.

These notes describe 1.1.0. If \`npm ls @idyeah/diya\` shows an older version, upgrade first; get_component says when each item arrived."
`;

exports[`what an agent reads, word for word > get_setup: vite 1`] = `
"# Set up @idyeah/diya 1.1.0 in Vite

## 1. Install
\`\`\`sh
npm install @idyeah/diya
\`\`\`

## 2. src/main.tsx (the entry)
\`\`\`tsx
import { StrictMode } from 'react'
import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client'
import { DiyaProvider } from '@idyeah/diya'
import '@idyeah/diya/styles.css'
import './index.css'
import App from './App'

createRoot(document.getElementById('root')!).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <DiyaProvider>
      <App />
    </DiyaProvider>
  </StrictMode>,
)
\`\`\`

## Rules
- Every component renders inside \`DiyaProvider\`; popups, tooltips and toasts need it. Its \`theme\` defaults to \`"system"\` (follows the OS light or dark setting, in CSS, with no flash); pass \`"light"\` or \`"dark"\` to fix it. It paints its own background and text color; \`surface={false}\` leaves that to your page.
- Fields work controlled (\`value\` with \`onValueChange\`; Switch: \`checked\` with \`onCheckedChange\`) or uncontrolled (\`defaultValue\`; Switch: \`defaultChecked\`). Native \`name\`, \`onChange\` and \`onBlur\` reach the native control, so react-hook-form \`register()\` works on TextInput, TextArea, Select, Switch, Choice and Slider without a Controller. Labels are required, even when hidden with \`hideLabel\`.
- Lay screens out with \`Stack\` (vertical) and \`Inline\` (horizontal, wrapping): \`gap\` takes a spacing step (1–8) or any CSS length, plus \`align\`, \`justify\`, \`wrap\` and \`as\`.
- One brand color, set once: \`<DiyaProvider brandColor="#1F4E7A">\`, or \`{ light, dark }\`. Components take no color props (chart series aside); \`tone\` picks a status.
- Every component takes \`className\`, \`style\` and its root element's attributes. Theme with public \`--diya-*\` tokens on \`.diya-root\`, never by overriding internal classes. DIYA's CSS sits in \`@layer diya\`, so your CSS and Tailwind utilities win.
- Links: items with \`href\` render the provider's \`linkComponent\` (such as Next.js \`Link\`, passed from a \`'use client'\` providers file) or a plain anchor. Button takes \`href\` and \`asChild\`. TextLink's \`href\` is always a plain anchor; for client-side routing, pass your router's link to it with \`asChild\`.
- DIYA ships no icon set. Pass any React icon (for example from lucide-react) to icon slots.
- Charts import from \`@idyeah/diya/charts\` and need \`echarts@6\` installed.
- Next.js App Router: DIYA components are client components; a file that passes functions as props needs \`'use client'\`.
- DIYA animates popups, dialogs, toggles and selection, and follows the device's Reduce Motion setting. \`motion="reduced"\` (fades only) or \`"off"\` on DiyaProvider changes it for everything inside; nested providers inherit it. Tune the speed with \`--diya-duration-scale\`. In browser tests, render with \`motion="off"\`.

These notes describe 1.1.0. If \`npm ls @idyeah/diya\` shows an older version, upgrade first; get_component says when each item arrived."
`;

exports[`what an agent reads, word for word > get_theme: #1F4E7A + glass 1`] = `
"# Theme for @idyeah/diya 1.1.0

\`\`\`tsx
<DiyaProvider brandColor="#1F4E7A" glass>
\`\`\`

That's the whole theme. DIYA works out the rest, so don't set these tokens yourself:

| Token | Light | Dark |
| --- | --- | --- |
| \`--diya-color-accent\` | \`#1F4E7A\` (text on it 8.3:1) | \`#1F4E7A\` (text on it 8.3:1) |
| \`--diya-color-accent-text\` | \`#FAFAFA\` | \`#FAFAFA\` |
| \`--diya-color-accent-soft\` | \`#1F4E7A1F\` | \`#1F4E7A33\` |
| \`--diya-color-accent-ink\` | \`#1F4E7A\` | \`#6E8CA7\` |

## Notes
- In Dark, #1F4E7A sits at 2.2:1 against the page (#111113), so solid buttons stand out less than DIYA's own; their labels still read. If you'd like them to stand out, dark could use #41698E: \`brandColor={{ light: '#1F4E7A', dark: '#41698E' }}\`.
- In Dark, brand-colored text uses #6E8CA7 so it reads at 4.5:1.

## Other settings
- Corners: \`--diya-corner-scale\` (0 square, 1 default, 2 round) scales every control radius.
- Font: \`fontFamily\` on the provider sets \`--diya-font\`.
- Glass: \`glass\` gives headers, popups and tabs a translucent, blurred finish.
- Anything else: public \`--diya-*\` tokens on \`.diya-root\` (list_tokens). Never override DIYA's internal \`.diya-*\` classes.
- Try it live: https://diya13.ai/explore (Customize)."
`;

